{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"ir-sensors","name":"Line, obstacle, laser and motion sensors","version":"1.1.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Sensors robots use: the TCRT5000 line sensor (sees dark lines on a light floor), the FC-51 obstacle sensor (IR, a few cm), the VL53L0X laser distance sensor (I2C, up to 2 m) and the HC-SR501 PIR motion sensor. They really look at the bench. Includes VL53L0X.h and Adafruit_VL53L0X.h.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// Sensors that look at the bench: a camera for the line sensor's reflection and the PIR's view,\r\n// a distance beam for the obstacle and laser sensors.\r\n\r\n/** how light a picture is: 0 (black) .. 1 (white), on average */\r\nfunction lightness(frame) {\r\n  let sum = 0;\r\n  const n = frame.width * frame.height;\r\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += 0.299 * frame.data[i * 4] + 0.587 * frame.data[i * 4 + 1] + 0.114 * frame.data[i * 4 + 2];\r\n  return sum / n / 255;\r\n}\r\n\r\n// TCRT5000: an IR LED shining down and a phototransistor seeing how much comes back. Light floors\r\n// reflect a lot (DO low, the module's LED lit), dark lines little (DO high).\r\nbench.device('tcrt5000', (part) => {\r\n  const eye = part.camera('eye');\r\n  const threshold = Number(part.params.threshold ?? 70) / 100;\r\n  let dark = 0, powered = false, isDark = false, seen = false;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v >= 3;\r\n      eye.want(powered ? 60 : 0); // (a real one answers in microseconds: as often as the app allows)\r\n      const f = eye.frame;\r\n      if (f) { dark = 1 - lightness(f); seen = true; }\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('DO'); io.release('AO'); io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      isDark = dark > threshold;\r\n      io.drive('DO', isDark ? v : 0, 1);\r\n      io.drive('AO', v * Math.max(0, Math.min(1, dark)), 1);\r\n      io.draw(0.02);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\r\n      if (!seen) return ['looking...'];\r\n      return [`${isDark ? 'dark (DO high)' : 'light (DO low)'}, ${Math.round(dark * 100)} % dark`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// FC-51: OUT low while something reflects its IR back from within its range.\r\nbench.device('fc51', (part) => {\r\n  const beam = part.ranger('beam');\r\n  const range = Number(part.params.range ?? 10);\r\n  let powered = false, near = false;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v >= 3;\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('OUT'); io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      const d = beam.distance;\r\n      near = d !== null && d <= range;\r\n      io.drive('OUT', near ? 0 : v, 1);\r\n      io.draw(0.025);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\r\n      const d = beam.distance;\r\n      return [`${near ? 'something there (OUT low)' : 'clear (OUT high)'}${d !== null ? `, nearest ${d.toFixed(1)} cm` : ''}`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// VL53L0X: a laser and a timer: how long its light takes to come back. On I2C at 0x29. The\r\n// registers a driver uses for a reading: 0xC0 model id (0xEE), 0x00 start, 0x13 interrupt status\r\n// (bit 0-2: a reading is ready), 0x0B clear interrupt, 0x14 range status, 0x1E-0x1F range (mm).\r\nbench.device('vl53l0x', (part) => {\r\n  const beam = part.ranger('beam');\r\n  let powered = false, reg = 0, mm = 8190, readings = 0, addr = 0x29;\r\n  return {\r\n    i2c: {\r\n      address: () => (powered ? addr : -1),\r\n      write(bytes) {\r\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\r\n        reg = bytes[0];\r\n        if (bytes.length > 1) {\r\n          if (reg === 0x8a) addr = bytes[1] & 0x7f; // (I2C_SLAVE_DEVICE_ADDRESS: the address can be changed)\r\n        }\r\n        return true;\r\n      },\r\n      read(n) {\r\n        const r = new Array(256).fill(0);\r\n        r[0xc0] = 0xee; r[0xc1] = 0xaa; r[0xc2] = 0x10;\r\n        r[0x13] = 0x04; // a reading is ready\r\n        r[0x14] = mm >= 8190 ? 0x00 : 0x58;\r\n        r[0x1e] = (mm >> 8) & 255; r[0x1f] = mm & 255;\r\n        if (reg === 0x1e) readings++;\r\n        const out = [];\r\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(r[(reg + i) & 255]);\r\n        return out;\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      powered = io.supply('VIN', 'GND') >= 2.6;\r\n      const d = beam.distance; // cm\r\n      mm = d === null || d > 200 ? 8190 : Math.max(30, Math.round(d * 10));\r\n      io.draw(powered ? 0.019 : 0);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\r\n      return [`${mm >= 8190 ? 'nothing in range' : `${mm} mm`}, I2C 0x${addr.toString(16)}, ${readings} readings`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// HC-SR501: it sees changes in the infrared in front of it (warm things moving). Here: changes in\r\n// what its camera sees. OUT stays high for the hold time after the last movement.\r\nbench.device('pir', (part) => {\r\n  const eye = part.camera('eye');\r\n  const hold = Number(part.params.hold ?? 3);\r\n  let prev = null, powered = false, since = 0, until = -1, high = false, triggers = 0, lastTime = -1;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      if (v >= 4.5 && !powered) since = io.time;\r\n      powered = v >= 4.5;\r\n      eye.want(powered ? 8 : 0);\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('OUT'); prev = null; high = false; io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      const f = eye.frame;\r\n      if (f && f.time !== lastTime) {\r\n        lastTime = f.time;\r\n        if (prev && io.time - since > 2) {\r\n          // how many of its pixels changed noticeably since the last picture\r\n          let changed = 0;\r\n          for (let i = 0; i < f.data.length; i += 4) {\r\n            const d = Math.abs(f.data[i] - prev[i]) + Math.abs(f.data[i + 1] - prev[i + 1]) + Math.abs(f.data[i + 2] - prev[i + 2]);\r\n            if (d > 40) changed++;\r\n          }\r\n          if (changed >= 2) {\r\n            if (!high) triggers++;\r\n            until = io.time + hold;\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n        prev = f.data.slice();\r\n      }\r\n      high = io.time < until;\r\n      io.drive('OUT', high ? 3.3 : 0, 1);\r\n      io.draw(0.00006);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC 5-12 V)'];\r\n      return [high ? 'movement! (OUT high)' : 'all still (OUT low)', `${triggers} times`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n","sketch":{"VL53L0X.h":{"classes":["VL53L0X"],"code":"// VL53L0X.h (Pololu's library), the parts sketches use: init(), setTimeout(), startContinuous(),\n// readRangeContinuousMillimeters(), readRangeSingleMillimeters(), timeoutOccurred(), setAddress().\n// It reads the sensor's real result registers (0x13 ready, 0x1E-0x1F the range in mm).\nclass VL53L0X {\n  constructor() {\n    this.address = 0x29;\n    this.timeout = 0;\n    this.didTimeout = false;\n    this.continuous = false;\n  }\n  setBus() {}\n  setAddress(a) { this.writeReg(0x8a, a & 0x7f); this.address = a & 0x7f; }\n  getAddress() { return this.address; }\n  setTimeout(ms) { this.timeout = ms; }\n  getTimeout() { return this.timeout; }\n  timeoutOccurred() { const t = this.didTimeout; this.didTimeout = false; return t; }\n  writeReg(r, v) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.address);\n    Wire.write(r);\n    Wire.write(v);\n    return Wire.endTransmission();\n  }\n  readRegs(r, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.address);\n    Wire.write(r);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.address, n) !== n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  /** true if a VL53L0X answers (model id 0xEE) */\n  init(io2v8 = true) {\n    const id = this.readRegs(0xc0, 1);\n    return !!id && id[0] === 0xee;\n  }\n  setMeasurementTimingBudget() { return true; }\n  setSignalRateLimit() { return true; }\n  startContinuous(period = 0) { this.writeReg(0x00, period ? 0x04 : 0x02); this.continuous = true; }\n  stopContinuous() { this.writeReg(0x00, 0x01); this.continuous = false; }\n  readRangeContinuousMillimeters() {\n    const start = millis();\n    for (;;) {\n      const st = this.readRegs(0x13, 1);\n      if (st && (st[0] & 0x07)) break;\n      if (!st || (this.timeout && millis() - start > this.timeout)) { this.didTimeout = true; return 65535; }\n      delay(1);\n    }\n    const r = this.readRegs(0x1e, 2);\n    this.writeReg(0x0b, 0x01); // clear \"ready\"\n    if (!r) { this.didTimeout = true; return 65535; }\n    return (r[0] << 8) | r[1];\n  }\n  readRangeSingleMillimeters() {\n    this.writeReg(0x00, 0x01);\n    delay(20); // (a reading takes about 30 ms on a real one)\n    return this.readRangeContinuousMillimeters();\n  }\n}\n"},"Adafruit_VL53L0X.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_VL53L0X","VL53L0X_RangingMeasurementData_t"],"code":"// Adafruit_VL53L0X.h, the usual parts: begin(), rangingTest(&measure, false) filling\n// measure.RangeMilliMeter and measure.RangeStatus (4 = out of range), readRange().\nclass VL53L0X_RangingMeasurementData_t {\n  constructor() { this.RangeMilliMeter = 0; this.RangeStatus = 4; }\n}\nclass Adafruit_VL53L0X {\n  constructor() { this.address = 0x29; }\n  regs(r, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.address);\n    Wire.write(r);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.address, n) !== n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  begin(addr = 0x29) {\n    this.address = addr;\n    Wire.begin();\n    const id = this.regs(0xc0, 1);\n    return !!id && id[0] === 0xee;\n  }\n  rangingTest(m, debug = false) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.address);\n    Wire.write(0x00);\n    Wire.write(0x01);\n    Wire.endTransmission();\n    delay(20);\n    const r = this.regs(0x1e, 2);\n    const mm = r ? (r[0] << 8) | r[1] : 8190;\n    if (m) {\n      m.RangeMilliMeter = mm;\n      m.RangeStatus = mm >= 8190 ? 4 : 0;\n    }\n    return 0;\n  }\n  readRange() {\n    const m = new VL53L0X_RangingMeasurementData_t();\n    this.rangingTest(m);\n    return m.RangeMilliMeter;\n  }\n  readRangeStatus() { return this.readRange() >= 8190 ? 4 : 0; }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"tcrt5000","name":"Line sensor (TCRT5000)","description":"Looks straight down (put it 0.5-2 cm above the floor, under a robot): DO is LOW over a light surface and HIGH over a dark line; AO gives more volts the darker it is. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND. Lines: dark plates or blocks on a light one.","swatch":"#1d4fb8","mass":3,"params":[{"key":"threshold","label":"Dark above (%) (its knob)","kind":"number","min":5,"max":95,"step":1}],"defaults":{"threshold":70},"shape":[{"box":[3,0.16,1.4],"at":[0,0.5,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"box":[0.6,0.5,1],"at":[1.1,0.17,0],"color":"#141416"},{"box":[0.5,0.5,0.5],"at":[-0.3,0.83,0.3],"color":"#2f7fd8","collide":false},{"camera":{"id":"eye","px":[4,4],"fov":40,"look":[0,-1,0],"range":8},"at":[1.1,0.4,0]}],"pins":[{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","at":[-1.4,0.66,0.381],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-1.4,0.66,0.127],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"DO","label":"DO (high = dark)","at":[-1.4,0.66,-0.127],"kind":"out"},{"id":"AO","label":"AO (analog)","at":[-1.4,0.66,-0.381],"kind":"out"}],"device":"tcrt5000"},{"id":"fc51","name":"Obstacle sensor (FC-51)","description":"An IR LED and a receiver looking forward (along +x, the way its LEDs point): OUT goes LOW when something is closer than its range (2-30 cm, its knob), HIGH otherwise. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND.","swatch":"#1d4fb8","mass":3,"params":[{"key":"range","label":"Range (cm) (its knob)","kind":"number","min":2,"max":30,"step":1}],"defaults":{"range":10},"shape":[{"box":[3.1,0.16,1.4],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"cyl":[0.25,0.6],"at":[1.6,0.4,0.3],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#d6d6d6"},{"cyl":[0.25,0.6],"at":[1.6,0.4,-0.3],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#141416"},{"ranger":{"id":"beam","look":[1,0,0],"max":40},"at":[1.95,0.4,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["OUT","GND","VCC"],"at":[-1.5,0,-0.254],"dir":"z","kinds":{"OUT":"out","GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"OUT":{"label":"OUT (low = something there)"}}}],"device":"fc51"},{"id":"vl53l0x","name":"Laser distance sensor (VL53L0X)","description":"Measures how far the first thing ahead is (along +x), 3 cm to 2 m, in millimetres, over I2C (address 0x29). VIN (3.3-5 V), GND, SCL, SDA. With VL53L0X.h: sensor.init(); sensor.startContinuous(); sensor.readRangeContinuousMillimeters(). 8190 = nothing in range.","swatch":"#7a3ec8","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.3,0.16,1.8],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#7a3ec8"},{"box":[0.45,0.2,0.25],"at":[0.4,0.26,0],"color":"#141416"},{"ranger":{"id":"beam","look":[1,0,0],"max":200},"at":[0.7,0.26,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VIN","GND","SCL","SDA"],"at":[-0.5,0,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"VIN":"vin","GND":"gnd","SCL":"i2c","SDA":"i2c"},"extra":{"VIN":{"label":"VIN (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.6,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"vl53l0x"},{"id":"pir","name":"Motion sensor (HC-SR501 PIR)","description":"Sees things move in front of it (along +x, a wide cone, a few metres): OUT goes high (3.3 V) for its hold time after it sees movement. VCC (5-12 V), GND. It needs a couple of seconds to settle when it gets power.","swatch":"#f2f2f2","mass":8,"params":[{"key":"hold","label":"Hold time (s)","kind":"number","min":1,"max":30,"step":0.5}],"defaults":{"hold":3},"shape":[{"box":[0.16,2.4,3.2],"at":[0,1.2,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"sphere":1.15,"at":[0.1,1.2,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[0.6,0.4,3.2],"at":[-0.3,0.2,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"camera":{"id":"eye","px":[16,12],"fov":100,"look":[1,0,0],"range":500},"at":[1.3,1.2,0]}],"pins":[{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (5-12 V)","at":[-0.5,0.4,0.254],"kind":"vin","vmin":4.5,"vmax":20},{"id":"OUT","at":[-0.5,0.4,0],"kind":"out"},{"id":"GND","at":[-0.5,0.4,-0.254],"kind":"gnd"}],"device":"pir"}],"examples":[{"name":"How far? (VL53L0X)","description":"A laser distance sensor looking at a block: the distance in the serial monitor. Drag the block while it runs.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"How far? (VL53L0X)","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-8,0,-4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"tof","type":"ir-sensors/vl53l0x","name":"VL53L0X","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"target","type":"block","name":"Target","params":{"w":2,"h":6,"d":8,"material":"wood","color":"#c98a4b"},"parent":null,"pos":[20,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"tof","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"tof","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"tof","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"tof","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// How far is the block? A VL53L0X laser sensor on I2C. Drag the block while it runs.\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <VL53L0X.h>\n\nVL53L0X sensor;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Wire.begin();\n  sensor.setTimeout(500);\n  if (!sensor.init()) {\n    Serial.println(\"No VL53L0X found: check its wires\");\n    while (1) delay(1000);\n  }\n  sensor.startContinuous();\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int mm = sensor.readRangeContinuousMillimeters();\n  if (sensor.timeoutOccurred()) Serial.println(\"timeout\");\n  else if (mm >= 8190) Serial.println(\"nothing in range\");\n  else {\n    Serial.print(mm);\n    Serial.println(\" mm\");\n  }\n  delay(500);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Obstacle and line","description":"An obstacle sensor and a line sensor lighting LEDs: the line sensor sits over a black strip on white, the obstacle sensor looks at a block. Drag things while it runs.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Obstacle and line","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"fc51","type":"ir-sensors/fc51","name":"Obstacle sensor","params":{"range":10},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,-10],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"wall","type":"block","name":"Something in the way","params":{"w":3,"h":5,"d":6,"material":"wood","color":"#c98a4b"},"parent":null,"pos":[10,0,-10],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"paper","type":"plate","name":"White paper","params":{"w":14,"h":0.3,"d":10,"material":"plastic","color":"#f4f4f2"},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,8],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"tape","type":"plate","name":"Black tape","params":{"w":2,"h":0.1,"d":10,"material":"plastic","color":"#151515"},"parent":{"uid":"paper","body":"body"},"pos":[3,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"line1","type":"ir-sensors/tcrt5000","name":"Line sensor over the tape","params":{"threshold":70},"parent":{"uid":"tape","body":"body"},"pos":[-1.1,0.05,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"line2","type":"ir-sensors/tcrt5000","name":"Line sensor over paper","params":{"threshold":70},"parent":{"uid":"paper","body":"body"},"pos":[-4,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"led1","type":"led","name":"Obstacle LED","params":{"color":"red"},"parent":null,"pos":[-4,0,-8],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"led2","type":"led","name":"Line LED","params":{"color":"green"},"parent":null,"pos":[-4,0,6],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"fc51","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"fc51","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"fc51","pin":"OUT"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"line1","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"line1","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"line1","pin":"DO"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"line2","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"line2","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP4"},"b":{"uid":"line2","pin":"DO"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP14"},"b":{"uid":"led1","pin":"A"},"color":"#f08c2a"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led1","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"led2","pin":"A"},"color":"#f08c2a"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led2","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// The red LED lights when something is in front of the obstacle sensor;\n// the green one when the first line sensor is over the black tape.\n#define OBSTACLE 2   // FC-51 OUT: LOW = something there\n#define LINE_A 3     // TCRT5000 DO: HIGH = dark\n#define LINE_B 4\n#define RED 14\n#define GREEN 15\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(OBSTACLE, INPUT);\n  pinMode(LINE_A, INPUT);\n  pinMode(LINE_B, INPUT);\n  pinMode(RED, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(GREEN, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  bool blocked = digitalRead(OBSTACLE) == LOW;\n  bool onLineA = digitalRead(LINE_A) == HIGH;\n  bool onLineB = digitalRead(LINE_B) == HIGH;\n  digitalWrite(RED, blocked);\n  digitalWrite(GREEN, onLineA);\n  Serial.print(blocked ? \"blocked\" : \"clear\");\n  Serial.print(\"  sensor A: \");\n  Serial.print(onLineA ? \"line\" : \"paper\");\n  Serial.print(\"  sensor B: \");\n  Serial.println(onLineB ? \"line\" : \"paper\");\n  delay(500);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Line-following robot","description":"A two-wheel robot with two line sensors under its nose follows an oval of black tape on paper. Press Run; drag the robot off the line and put it back on.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Line-following robot","parts":[{"uid":"chassis","type":"plate","name":"Chassis","params":{"w":12,"h":0.3,"d":9,"material":"plastic","color":"#8fa3b8"},"parent":null,"pos":[-12,4.550000000000001,35],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"motorR","type":"motor-tt","name":"Right motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,-0.15,3.55],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"motorL","type":"motor-tt","name":"Left motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[3.2,-0.15,-3.55],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelR","type":"wheel","name":"Right wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorR","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,1,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelL","type":"wheel","name":"Left wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorL","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"battery","type":"battery-18650","name":"Batteries","params":{"count":"2","charge":100},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-2.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"brain","type":"maker-board","name":"Brain","params":{"usb":false},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[2.6,0.15,0],"rot":[0,-0.7071,0,0.7071]},{"uid":"driver","type":"drv8833","name":"Motor driver","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"battery","body":"body"},"pos":[0,2,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"caster","type":"caster","name":"Caster","params":{"r":1.57},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-4.6,-0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"bracket","type":"block","name":"Sensor bracket","params":{"w":1.4,"h":3.1,"d":5,"material":"plastic","color":"#d8dce4"},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[5,-3.25,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"lineL","type":"ir-sensors/tcrt5000","name":"Left line sensor","params":{"threshold":35},"parent":{"uid":"bracket","body":"body"},"pos":[0.2,-2.15,-0.75],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"lineR","type":"ir-sensors/tcrt5000","name":"Right line sensor","params":{"threshold":35},"parent":{"uid":"bracket","body":"body"},"pos":[0.2,-2.15,0.75],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"paper","type":"plate","name":"Paper","params":{"w":150,"h":0.3,"d":100,"material":"ca